      "created_at": "2025-05-30T13:04:27Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-05-30T13:04:27Z",
      "body": "I think you did not quite understand what things you have to specify \ud83d\ude04 \nYou don't need to specify the hostnames from docker and rather the hostname to connect to the docker socket / proxy. (and the port of that one). In the end it should have the same amount of hostnames and ports. \n\nSee https://github.com/apocas/dockerode#getting-started\nWe support host and port as parameters.\n\nBut I agree that in the future this should also be possible through the UI instead. (So like a normal integration)\nIt also seems like it is currently not possible to have the docker socket and an external docker proxy available at the same time.\n",
