      "body": "No, what I see is my Docker containers for localhost only. What I was hoping to do was have a new board in Homarr where I can show the containers from multiple hosts. So I would like to see a column for localhost, a column for 192.168.0.15 (as I've tried to add here), and then further columns for more hostnames or IP addresses.\n\nI thought that was what you meant above when you said in https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/3266#issuecomment-2920168050  _It should already be possible to add multiple docker integrations_.\n\nSo when you say do it manually, will this allow me to show two or more hosts and their containers? If so, please can you point me to some instructions?\n\nSo I'm still not really sure if showing containers from more than one host is supported, either through the GUI or manually and, if manually, then how and where do I configure it please?\n\nThanks and sorry if I've missed something obvious.",
